.Sh CPUID CONFIGURATION
The bhyve hypervisor allows for fine-grained manipulation of the complete set
of information returned by the x86
.Sy CPUID
instruction to a guest VM.
By default, the values returned are based on those of the host CPU.
.Pp
.Sy CPUID
information is structured by numbered
.Sy functions
.Po sometimes also referred to as
.Sq Sy leaves
.Pc .
Some
.Sy functions
support multiple
.Sy indices .
The corresponding values are returned in the 4 CPU registers
.Sy EAX ,
.Sy EBX ,
.Sy ECX ,
and
.Sy EDX .
.Pp
The bhyve hypervisor imposes a number of constraints on explicit modifications
of the information returned by the
.Sy CPUID
instruction:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It immutable
Bits in a register that may not be changed from the value set by the hypervisor
or the host CPU, e.g. feature bits corresponding to features that must remain
enabled or disabled for correct guest operation.
.It clear-only
Bits which may only be cleared if set by the hypervisor or the host CPU, e.g.
feature bits corresponding to instruction set extensions which may not be
enabled if unsupported by the host CPU.
.It lower-only
Bitmasks whose numerical value may only be lowered respective to the value set
by the hypervisor or the host CPU, e.g. values related to cache and TLB sizes.
.El
.Pp
The bhyve hypervisor also applies a number of automatic fixups to the provided
CPUID configuration:
.Bl -bullet
.It
ensure consistency across all vCPUs with the configured CPU topology
.It
remove unreachable CPUID functions based on the CPUID-region specific maximum
levels
.It
clear and/or propagate CPUID information according to CPU vendor rules
.El
.Pp
The following variables can be used to modify the behaviour of the
.Sy CPUID
emulation:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va cpuid . Ns Va check
Set the default constraints check behaviour for the CPUID configuration:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It none
Disable all constraints checks.
.It warn
Warn about constraints violations.
.It fail
Warn about constraints violations and abort the guest startup.
.It fix
Warn about constraints violations and automatically fix them.
.El
.It Va cpuid . Ns Va fallback-style
Set the fallback style to use when an unsupported
.Sy CPUID
function or index is requested.
.Pp
The following fallback styles are supported:
.Bl -column "intel" "Intel-style fallback"
.It Sy Name Ta Sy Fallback-Style Ta Description
.It Sy amd Ta AMD-style fallback Ta
Return all zeros for unsupported
.Sy CPUID
functions.
.It Sy intel Ta Intel-style fallback Ta
Return information for the highest numbered supported
.Sy CPUID
function.
.El
By default, the appropriate fallback style for the CPU vendor is used.
.El
.Pp
The following variables can be used to modify the information returned by the
.Sy CPUID
instruction:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va cpuid . Ns Va hypervisor
The hypervisor identification, a 12-character string returned by CPUID function
.Sy 0x40000000
in registers
.Sy EBX ,
.Sy ECX ,
and
.Sy EDX .
Whitespaces at the end of the string are significant.
If the assigned string is less than 12 characters in length, it will be padded
with
.Sy nul
characters.
.Pp
The following short-hand aliases for well-known hypervisor identifications are
supported:
.Bl -column "virtualbox" "Identification"
.It Sy Alias Ta Sy Identification Ta Sy Hypervisor
.It hyperv Ta Dq Microsoft\~Hv Ta
Microsoft Hyper-V
.It kvm Ta Dq KVMKVMKVM Ta
Linux KVM
.It virtualbox Ta Dq VBoxVBoxVBox Ta
Oracle VirtualBox
.It vmware Ta Dq VMwareVMware Ta
VMware ESXi
.It xen Ta Dq XenVMMXenVMM Ta
Xen
.El
.Pp
The default value is
.Dq bhyve\~bhyve\~ .
.It Va cpuid . Ns Va vendor
The CPU vendor identification, a 12-character string returned by CPUID function
.Sy 0x00000000
in registers
.Sy EBX ,
.Sy EDX ,
and
.Sy ECX .
Whitespaces at the end of the string are significant.
If the assigned string is less than 12 characters in length, it will be padded
with
.Sy nul
characters.
.Pp
The following short-hand aliases for well-known CPU vendor identifications are
supported:
.Bl -column "virtualbox" "Identification"
.It Sy Alias Ta Sy Identification Ta Sy CPU Vendor
.It amd Ta Dq AuthenticAMD Ta
AMD
.It intel Ta Dq GenuineIntel Ta
Intel
.El
.It Va cpuid . Ns Va family
The CPU family number.
If not set, this defaults to 6 for Intel CPUs and 15
.Pq 0xf
for AMD CPUs.
.It Va cpuid . Ns Va model
The CPU model number
If not set, this defaults to 15
.Pq 0xf
for Intel CPUs and 6 for AMD CPUs.
.It Va cpuid . Ns Va stepping
The CPU stepping.
If not set, this defaults to 1.
.It Va cpuid . Ns Va brand
The CPU Brand String, a 48-character string returned by CPUID functions
.Sy 0x80000002 ,
.Sy 0x80000003 ,
and
.Sy 0x80000004 .
Whitespaces at the end of the string are significant.
If the assigned string is less than 48 characters in length, it will be padded
with
.Sy nul
characters.
.It Va cpuid . Ns Va features
A comma separated list of CPU features to enable or disable.
To disable a feature, prefix the feature name with a
.Sq -
sign.
Features are enabled and disabled in the order specified.
If a features is specified multiple times for enabling and disabling,
the final specification is used.
.Pp
